A NOTE ON WHAT A LICENCE MEANS HERE
-----------------------------------
Under Australian law, facts are not protected by copyright (IceTV v Nine
Network) and computer-generated compilations attract no copyright at all
(Telstra v Phone Directories). Australia has no sui generis database right.

So this licence is best understood as the attribution norm we ask you to
honour, rather than a claim of ownership over facts about racetracks and
greyhounds. Please credit it anyway: attribution is what keeps open data
coming.
